      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "Lipophilic basic antihistamines such as hydroxyzine readily cross the BBB, but the query guanethidine is far more polar and strongly ionized, so this evidence does not overcome its known poor CNS penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is guanethidine, a strongly basic, largely ionized guanidine that is classically considered to have poor blood-brain barrier penetration and acts peripherally. The supportive records involve more lipophilic CNS drugs or guanidines with specialized transport, and none provide direct evidence of meaningful CNS access for this exact molecule.",
